### 3. `PostingController.java` — **[MODIFY]**

**Path:** `freelance/.../features/posting/web/PostingController.java`

**Two changes:**

#### Change A — inject `MatchService`
Add to the controller's constructor-injected fields:
```java
private final MatchService matchService;
```
(`UserRepository` is already present in the controller.)

#### Change B — compute scores on `GET /postings`
Add `@AuthenticationPrincipal UserDetails userDetails` as a parameter to `getAllPostings()`.
After `Page<PostingTileDto> postings = postingService.getPostings(...)`:

```java
if (userDetails != null) {
    User currentUser = userRepository.findByUsername(userDetails.getUsername()).orElse(null);
    if (currentUser != null && currentUser.isFreelancer()) {
        postings.forEach(tile ->
            tile.setMatchPercentage(
                matchService.computeMatch(tile.getId(), currentUser.getId())
            )
        );
    }
}
```

- Unauthenticated callers → `userDetails` is null → skip → all `matchPercentage` stay null.
- Authenticated clients → `!isFreelancer()` → skip.
- `tile.getId()` is `UUID` from `PostingTileDto.id`. `currentUser.getId()` is the `User.id` UUID from `BaseEntity`.

#### Change C — new endpoint `GET /postings/{id}/match`
```java
@GetMapping("/{id}/match")
public ResponseEntity<Map<String, Integer>> getMatchScore(
        @PathVariable UUID id,
        @AuthenticationPrincipal UserDetails userDetails) {
    if (userDetails == null) return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of());
    User user = userRepository.findByUsername(userDetails.getUsername()).orElse(null);
    if (user == null || !user.isFreelancer()) return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of());
    Integer score = matchService.computeMatch(id, user.getId());
    if (score == null) return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of());
    return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of("matchPercentage", score));
}
```

Returns an empty map `{}` (not 404) for non-freelancers — easier for the frontend to handle gracefully.


